ear in Great Britain, split by road type \n\n Road traffic by road type table \n\n Billion vehicle miles travelled each year in Great Britain, split by road type \n\n| Year Year | A-roads A-roads | Minor roads Minor roads | Motorways Motorways |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 2025 | 151.6 | 119.0 | 71.9 |\n| 2024 | 148.7 | 117.2 | 70.2 |\n| 2023 | 145.6 | 115.4 | 69.9 |\n| 2022 | 142.0 | 113.5 | 68.2 |\n| 2021 | 129.7 | 107.6 | 60.3 |\n| 2020 | 115.4 | 97.8 | 52.7 |\n| 2019 | 150.2 | 117.9 | 70.5 |\n| 2018 | 148.6 | 116.6 | 69.0 |\n| 2017 | 146.5 | 117.4 | 68.7 |\n| 2016 | 144.9 | 115.4 | 67.7 |\n| 2015 | 141.0 | 112.9 | 66.5 |\n| 2014 | 138.5 | 111.2 | 64.8 |\n| 2013 | 135.8 | 106.6 | 63.3 |\n| 2012 | 135.8 | 106.4 | 62.4 |\n| 2011 | 137.0 | 105.5 | 61.8 |\n| 2010 | 136.4 | 105.8 | 61.0 |\n| 2009 | 138.2 | 107.3 | 61.8 |\n| 2008 | 138.5 | 109.8 | 62.2 |\n| 2007 | 139.7 | 111.1 | 62.5 |\n| 2006 | 140.5 | 108.1 | 61.8 |\n| 2005 | 138.6 | 106.9 | 60.3 |\n| 2004 | 139.2 | 106.4 | 60.0 |\n| 2003 | 137.3 | 106.9 | 57.8 |\n| 2002 | 135.8 | 106.8 | 57.6 |\n| 2001 | 133.7 | 103.4 | 56.4 |\n| 2000 | 131.5 | 103.1 | 54.9 |\n| 1999 | 132.1 | 103.5 | 54.6 |\n| 1998 | 130.5 | 101.1 | 53.3 |\n| 1997 | 129.0 | 99.8 | 51.0 |\n| 1996 | 127.0 | 98.5 | 48.6 |\n| 1995 | 124.0 | 97.1 | 45.9 |\n| 1994 | 121.2 | 96.8 | 44.0 |\n| 1993 | 118.5 | 95.4 | 42.4 |\n\n## Road traffic by country \n\n### Road traffic by country in 2025 \n\n#### England \n\n 292.6 bvm \n\n Up 1.9% from 2024 \n\n Up 1.1% from 2019 \n\n#### Scotland \n\n 30.8 bvm \n\n Up 1.3% from 2024 \n\n Up 2.5% from 2019 \n\n#### Wales \n\n 19.2 bvm \n\n Up 2.3% from 2024 \n\n Little change from 2019 \n\n### Road traffic by country from 1993 to 2025 \n\n Billion vehicle miles travelled each year in Great Britain, split by country \n\n Road traffic by country table \n\n Billion vehicle miles travelled each year in Great Britain, split by country \n\n| Year Year | England England | Scotland Scotland | Wales Wales |\n| --- | --- | ---